 evidence['reviveEquipmentSeparation']=dict(status='Immutable accepted-death numeric effects captured independently of loot; live NPC stat/proc attachment unfinished',policy='tools/reference/revive-equipment-deviation.json',captureReceipt='tools/reference/revive-before-death-native-evidence.json',activationReceipt='tools/reference/revive-native-activation-evidence.json',lifecycleReceipt='tools/reference/revive-native-lifecycle-evidence.json',originalGearRemainsLoot=True,itemClonesCreated=False,recipientLevels=99,completeNpcStatConsumer=False,nativeAbilityClockRestore=False)
 evidence['numericOperationGaps']=[dict(feature='Base enhanced-damage rounding',status='Legacy double source and current integer implementation differ in720source controls;modern executable parity unresolved;existing base ED behavior preserved'),dict(feature='By-time operations6/7',status='Current asymmetric channel targets retained in source metadata;time/environment services and native consumers remain unimplemented'),dict(feature='Full property17parameter-zero fallback generation',status='Source writer fallback is recorded;native named/ordinary zero-parameter range rolling remains outside numeric reader acceptance')]
 lines += ['', '## Recipient-level numeric suppliers','', 'The prepared original-item reader now takes an explicit recipient level for ordinary and named properties, local armor and weapon endpoints. Its life/mana suppliers retain FP256 fractions. Four source to-hit properties (`att/lvl`, `att%/lvl`, `att-dem/lvl`, `att-und/lvl`) use halves rather than the eighths used by the other registered scaled properties. See [scoped native evidence](../tools/reference/npc-item-suppliers-native-evidence.json). This is a numeric reader, not a complete NPC stat graph or combat/event consumer.','', '`dmg%/lvl` now uses the dedicated `dmg-max%` field, with a separate maximum calculation after ordinary ED and flat maximum damage. Actual Reaver/Eaglehorn equipment, weapon packets/strikes and original-item reloads verify the correction; see [maximum damage acceptance](../tools/reference/item-maximum-operations-native-evidence.json). The former numeric-reader rejection is removed. Full NPC stat application, callbacks and item procs remain unfinished. Existing base-ED integer rounding remains unchanged while its modern parity is uncertain; by-time operations6/7 and property17 parameter-zero fallback generation remain separate gaps. Named acquisition decisions are unchanged.','']
 lines += ['', '## Original-item stat attachment','', 'The prepared C# graph matches the source posting/removal/owner/damage-toggle policy over 12,288 contexts and exact ordered service traces. An explicit adapter wraps actual bound original items and recipients, copies caller-supplied stat arrays and requires recalculation/propagation services. Native original armor/sword fixtures pass attachment, repeat, damage toggle and removal before and after two world reloads. Their aggregate is deliberately a fixture service; no live NPC life/defense/damage setter or automatic full-stat projection is certified. The transient graph is not serialized or replayed. Multi-item ordering, cycles, reentrancy, real recipient-level mapping and complete stat operations remain unfinished. See [scoped attachment acceptance](../tools/reference/item-stat-attachment-native-evidence.json).','']
 lines += ['', '## Numeric stat graph','', 'The prepared numeric service now supplies recursive queries, dependency recalculation, propagation and base setters to the ownership graph. Source-assembled metadata covers 368 rows; 4,784 fields and every row ordinal match the owned build. Native results match 105,984 queries and 480 six-stage update cases from 23 complete source routines, including layered keys and value-change callbacks. Actual original armor/sword suppliers enter and leave transient numeric graphs before and after two reloads. The item projection is still explicitly supplied, with no live NPC stat setter or automatic graph replay. Player ModStats registration and world-time/class mapping remain outside the NPC adapter. By-time arithmetic is source-verified under declared clock angles; the world-time item consumer is still unfinished. See [numeric graph acceptance](../tools/reference/item-stat-values-native-evidence.json).','']
 lines += ['', '## Raw NPC property writers','', 'Saved original numeric property rolls now use 191 source-derived writer plans. All 284 property plans are inventoried; 93 plans remain outside this raw NPC writer adapter, including special/skill/event/socket functions. This is separate from existing player support and named acquisition eligibility. The machine inventory lists every omitted code and function. Fifteen complete source routines match 45,840 native dispatch/base-reset/ethereal cases and exact write traces; all 7,952 func/stat/set/val fields and 32 selected base fields match owned data.','', 'Real original Spirit Forge armor and an ordinary sword exercise saved-roll projection, raw per-level coefficients, recipient-level calculations, removal and two actual reloads. The armor explicitly reports its socket writer omission. Original items are never rerolled; unrepresented zero-parameter or shared-zero fallback rolls are reported rather than invented. Crafted/material/socket contents, quality initialization and conditional named-piece stats remain explicit omissions. Base arrays/type metadata remain caller inputs, and full creation/ethereal order plus modern low-ED fallback/base-reset parity still need corroboration before live NPC integration. See [raw writer acceptance](../tools/reference/item-property-writers-native-evidence.json).','']
 lines += ['', '## Revive equipment and loot separation','', 'Approved Revive behavior keeps original equipped gear lootable and stores its numeric effects independently, without cloning items or returning them to the NPC. Accepted-death snapshots retain gear rolls and recipient-level numeric views after the physical loot is moved or deleted. Prepared activation restores the original NPC and detaches its corpse lease before cleanup, preserving loot rights and preventing the old consumed corpse from shadowing the living unit identity. These paths do not yet apply a complete NPC equipment stat graph, conditional set effects or proc/event dispatch. Native ability-clock data are archived; restore/aging policy and custom timers remain unfinished. See [capture evidence](../tools/reference/revive-before-death-native-evidence.json), [activation evidence](../tools/reference/revive-native-activation-evidence.json) and [approved equipment decision](../tools/reference/revive-equipment-deviation.json).','']
